    {
      "sha256": "c1b1689777cc1528dadfacccfa0f9fbc595d214f887212aaf59f0753946ef4c9",
      "identification": "GitHub Advisory Database source archive",
      "verdict": "BENIGN",
      "evidence": [
        "Streamed all 788480 tar members. All 394137 advisory JSON files parse as schema 1.4.0 GHSA records with prose details, affected packages, severity and references. The remaining ten regular files are repository documents and five GitHub maintenance workflows.",
        "GHSA-hjq4-87xh-g4fv places a pickle reducer and bash reverse shell in details as a fenced vLLM exploit demonstration. The JSON does not execute that code.",
        "GHSA-w48f-wwwf-f5fr describes plugin configuration abuse through a quoted curl PoC; GHSA-3f7w-p8vr-4v5f describes an uploaded Jinja template and quotes the expression that would execute on a vulnerable target.",
        "Reviewed all 61 high-finding advisory members. PHP echo fragments, HTML handlers, marker writes and interpreter commands occur in report examples, not an archive install/launch path.",
        "Workflow scripts signal PR events, validate PR/branch data, and use GitHub APIs to create staging branches, retarget PRs and clean stale branches. These operations match repository maintenance. No repository-content execution path was found."
      ],
      "context_missing": "The archive capture is not pinned to an upstream commit. The benign judgment follows the inert data and reviewed maintenance code, without assuming an endpoint deployment.",
      "before": {
        "probability": 0.995,
        "calibrated_level": 25,
        "alert": true,
        "reported_units": 23722,
        "high_finding_counts": {
