    {
      "sha256": "491fff5aa289e45b3b8db178585e796730a9c0f4b442e76df57303767316ab7c",
      "identification": "Damaged native StormAttack resource DLL injector",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "evidence": [
        "CRT entry reaches mode dispatch at 0x401cb0. The mode branches reach service/DLL installation, Active Setup self-copy or DLL injection and cleanup.",
        "0x401150 selects calc/notepad/IE, creates the target, allocates/writes remote memory, resolves kernel32 LoadLibraryA and passes that export and the remote DLL path to CreateRemoteThread at 0x40123d.",
        "0x401260 opens HKLM LanmanServer Parameters, deletes ServiceDLL at 0x401320, and replaces it as REG_EXPAND_SZ at 0x40133e.",
        "0x401900 writes an Active Setup StubPath at 0x401a4b, reads its own image, patches mode/path fields, writes a self-copy at 0x401b26 and starts it.",
        "0x401390 obtains its module path, converts it to a short path, obtains COMSPEC and creates a /c del shell for self-deletion.",
        "0x402460 contains resource extraction and file writing. The .rsrc section is 40032 zero bytes and the IAT retains bound addresses. These damaged bytes do not negate surviving attack code, but do not establish successful DLL installation or DDoS execution."
      ],
      "context_missing": "No runtime success or working DLL payload is established. There is no supported WannaCry attribution.",
      "trait_changes": "None needed for the firing StormAttack behavior traits.",
      "before": {
        "probability": 0.99,
        "calibrated_level": 25,
        "alert": true,
        "reported_units": 1,
