    {
      "sha256": "62b35d86498d9eefbd5d6acd48c2c65856b082bc24803dcd26fa107a63948459",
      "identification": "UPX-packed Go overwrite infector containing GravityRAT GX images",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "evidence": [
        "UPX unpacking recovers a 14671002-byte Go executable. In main, filepath.Walk over C:\\Program Files reaches main.visit at 0x62c450.",
        "visit reads a selected file at 0x62c5e3, obtains mutated self bytes at 0x62c626, and overwrites the selected path with ioutil.WriteFile at 0x62c679. Generation marks, random padding and additional .exe copies follow.",
        "get_self_mutated_bytes at 0x62cf80 decodes an embedded Base64 PE, appends its bytes to the image and appends randomized padding.",
        "plant_start_up at 0x62cba0 creates randomized self-copy paths, writes mutation/generation-marked images at 0x62cd8e and calls add_startup at 0x62cdbd. add_startup targets Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run.",
        "main constructs randomized HTTP requestbin callbacks and calls net/http.(*Client).Get at 0x62d5dc. This is a reachable HTTP operation; its response is not shown to deliver commands.",
        "The PE at outer file offset 0x253a08 identifies itself through CLR metadata as LSASS 1.9. Its SHA-256 exactly matches Talos GX: 1c0ea462f0bbd7acfdf4c6daf3cb8ce09e1375b766fbd3ff89f40c0aa3f4fc96. Forager independently recovered that published binary and provenance.",
        "GX Program.Main initializes Services.Start, selects active HTTP domains and schedules tasks. Core.Manager.UpdateServer parses received tasks. CmdManager.DoViaCmd builds hidden cmd.exe /c commands with redirected output, starts the process and waits for the output file.",
        "GX UsbManager watches Win32_LogicalDisk insertion, selects files by extension and stages them. UploadManager reaches Agent.UploadFile, which uses WebClient.UploadFileTaskAsync with a signature-hash parameter to the GX endpoint.",
        "GX CpuTemp queries MSAcpi_ThermalZoneTemperature and returns a VM indication on Not supported. BIOS, system, processor/core and MAC checks corroborate its anti-VM purpose.",
        "The neighboring assembly at 0x2af040 is the legitimate Mono.Cecil library. Independent scanning does not attribute GravityRAT to that library. Carved GX unit names containing Mono.Cecil.dll are extractor labels, not the assembly identity."
      ],
      "context_missing": "The Go infection and persistence code independently establish malware. Execution of every embedded GX image and live C2 success are not asserted. The collector Glassworm/Snatch label is not supported family attribution.",
      "before": {
        "probability": 0.99,
        "calibrated_level": 25,
        "alert": true,
        "reported_units": 42,
