    "effect": "The three anti-static consumers require source/package contexts; the removed PE/ELF/Mach-O measurement was ineligible there. CrystalX used the C2 directory as a suppression, so GX/Storm and external GX controls were checked for new misattribution. The new size/count fact adds no distinct role to the existing metadata/binary downgrade selector.",
    "suppression_groups": "The Jinja builtins consumer already excludes all detection tools. Its replacement offensive-example group retains the same non-detector members, while websec-validator and teler remain covered by that existing directory exclusion. Other old suppression alternatives remain. Documentation grouping avoids broadening archive scope.",
    "http_get_consumers": "Reviewed the exact Go polling-agent consumer and ancestor selectors. The polling-agent rule additionally requires task/result routines, Client.Do, exec.Command and a literal HTTP IP endpoint; the infector does not satisfy that command-channel profile."
  },
